[00:01.04]Life, like a mist, appears for just a day,
[00:06.46]Then disappears tomorrow.
[00:14.22]All that we are can quickly fade away,
[00:20.76]Replaced with tears and sorrow.
[00:27.94]If a man should die, can he live again?
[00:34.84]Hear the promise God has made:
[00:39.37](Chorus)
[00:39.52]He will call; The dead will answer.
[00:47.60]They will live at his command.
[00:53.21]For he will have a longing
[00:59.76]For the work of his own hand.
[01:04.00]So have faith, and do not wonder,
[01:05.69]For our God can make us stand.
[01:07.24]And we will live forever,
[01:08.58]As the work of his own hand.
[01:10.00]Friends of our God, though they may pass away,
[01:12.60]Will never be forsaken.
[01:13.84]All those asleep who in God’s mem’ry stay,
[01:20.18]From death he will awaken.
[01:21.57]Then we’ll come to see all that life can be:
[01:23.75]Paradise eternally.
[01:24.72](Chorus)
[01:24.87]He will call; The dead will answer.
[01:26.65]They will live at his command.
[01:28.24]For he will have a longing
[01:29.26]For the work of his own hand.
[02:05.58]So have faith, and do not wonder,
[02:09.44]For our God can make us stand.
[02:10.86]And we will live forever,
[02:38.44]As the work of his own hand.
